      "writtenOn": "2026-01-28T21:43:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The existing logic explicitly states that the pgood input overrides the enable output, so this is working as expected. What platform are seeing this behavior on?\n\nIf the pgood GPIO doesn\u0027t actually indicate if the fan is powered, then the board should just delete the `pgood_gpio` node property and then the `faninfo` command will skip the pgood check.",
      "parentUuid": "3dc033dd_65536d22",
      "revId": "53ae87dd0fe1aeb30893e6558652357970f5f79e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
